{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The cycles of the graph, and every vertex’s tail, root and preimages. O(n) time, with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allocation per vertex. The result holds 5n + 3 ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s (two ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arrays for the preimage","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rows, one for the vertices by depth, a 12-byte record per vertex and a 4-byte preorder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number beside each vertex by depth), plus one per cycle and one per unit of the longest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tail; building it takes 3n more for a moment (two 12-byte entries per vertex).","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cycleDecomposition"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"FunctionalGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18CycleDecompositionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CycleDecomposition"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"CycleDecomposition.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/FunctionalGraphs\/CycleDecomposition.swift#L269"},"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18cycleDecompositionAC05CycleE0VyF","extendedModule":"FunctionalGraphs","title":"cycleDecomposition()","modules":[{"name":"FunctionalGraphs"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/cycleDecomposition()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cycleDecomposition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph","text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition","text":"CycleDecomposition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18CycleDecompositionV"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A counting sort of f gives the preimage rows and the in-degrees. Peeling the vertices of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in-degree zero, repeatedly, visits the tree vertices leaves first, summing subtree sizes on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the way, and leaves exactly the cyclic ones; each cycle is then walked from its least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex. Revisiting the peeled vertices in reverse, parents first, gives every tail length"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and root and a preorder numbering of the trees from the subtree sizes; a counting sort by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"depth then lays out the level-ancestor table. Nothing recurses or chases a chain of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependent reads, so a tail of 10⁷ vertices needs no call stack."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph has fewer than 2³¹ vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph\/cycledecomposition()"]}],"references":{"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs/FunctionalGraph/CycleDecomposition":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CycleDecomposition"}],"title":"FunctionalGraph.CycleDecomposition","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph\/cycledecomposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CycleDecomposition"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every cycle of a functional graph, and for each vertex its tail and the cycle it reaches, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Flajolet and Odlyzko’s terms: walking from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":", the first vertex on a cycle is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"tailLength(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" steps away (Sage’s “preperiod”), on a cycle of "},{"code":"cycleLength(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices. For a permutation, "},{"code":"cycles","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is its cycle decomposition and every tail is zero."}]},"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"FunctionalGraphs","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs"},"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs/FunctionalGraph/cycleDecomposition()":{"title":"cycleDecomposition()","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph\/cycledecomposition()","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/cycleDecomposition()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cycleDecomposition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV","text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18CycleDecompositionV","text":"CycleDecomposition","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The cycles of the graph, and every vertex’s tail, root and preimages. O(n) time, with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allocation per vertex. The result holds 5n + 3 "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"s (two "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" arrays for the preimage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows, one for the vertices by depth, a 12-byte record per vertex and a 4-byte preorder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number beside each vertex by depth), plus one per cycle and one per unit of the longest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tail; building it takes 3n more for a moment (two 12-byte entries per vertex)."}]},"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs/FunctionalGraph":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph of a function f on the vertices "},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": every vertex "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has exactly one out-edge,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"v → f(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a fixed point is a self-loop. Also called a successor graph (Laaksonen,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook"}]},{"type":"text","text":", §16.3)."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"FunctionalGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"identifier"}]}}}